# On layouts/push-out.jsonc an asteroid field of radius 100 lies at (2000, 2000) between two destroyers. Near is ordered
# to a point 5 outside the field's edge, Deep to a point 40 inside it. Near's point lies in the cells the planner costs
# around the field but not in its impassable core, so Near has a path (the cells the core touches reach 125 from the
# center, the point is 105): it flies in until it meets the field and the push-out moves it straight back out by
# position to the field's radius plus its own model radius (about 113 from the center), keeping its velocity. Near's
# point lies 8 beyond that ring: the brake spring slows the ship pressed there to about 5, below half its impulse speed
# (10), so the arrival test ends its order (move=none) and it comes to rest. Deep's point lies inside the field's
# impassable core: the game's planner has no path to a goal in an impassable cell, so Deep holds where it stands with
# no order (move=none) and never meets the field. (A move order cannot press a ship against the ring with its
# order open: every point within the ring is in the core.)
# Dumps: "before" shows both 500 from the field's center; "driving" Near on its way with move=<x>,<z> and Deep holding
# with move=none; "edge" and "later" (10 s on) show Near at the ring with move=none and Deep still 500 from the center.
# Run it with --layout layouts/push-out.jsonc; the layout's header comment has the whole command.
# The points are in the frame of the dump's pos= field, whose z is the layout z mirrored.
wait 1
dump before
select Near
wait 0.3
move 1895 -2000
select Deep
wait 0.3
move 2060 -2000
wait 3
dump driving
wait 30
dump edge
wait 10
dump later
